Advanced study of recovery and whole-life functional equivalence (@mat-selection-recovery-study: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @materials-engineering, #source "../sources/Life-Cycle-Assessment-Detailed-Guide-ILCD.lingua#r_6YXH2DKX7XZRCE6XSCJ2QGJ3YX", #source "../../../materials/metals-and-metallurgical-production/sources/Metal-Recycling-UNEP-IRP.lingua#r_40JXFY43ST442BB8MJEAYJT9N1", #source "../sources/Materials-Science-behind-Sustainable-Metals-Raabe.lingua#r_6MXWN12M466MS374XY585GBHBN", #source "../sources/Plastics-Recycling-Economy-NIST.lingua#r_4FMXC9V02YNV4DFSCCV0CVR8JN", #source "../sources/Recycled-Concrete-Aggregates-McNeil-Kang.lingua#r_7RV5XYMDWNA5KPVRYC7052WV8E", #source "../sources/Wood-Handbook-FPL-2021.lingua#r_2SP2KMHCD78MQGZN69GKPGJ3WM", #materials-engineering "Defend-the-selection-service-and-recovery-account.lingua#r_3EKGFH7N9TS7SSRZHCP0MX6E8W") { r_1GK297HPGAR04W9W368BXG1HR8
**Read:** [Life-cycle assessment, detailed guidance — ILCD Handbook](../sources/Life-Cycle-Assessment-Detailed-Guide-ILCD.lingua#r_6YXH2DKX7XZRCE6XSCJ2QGJ3YX) in full; [Metal Recycling: Opportunities, Limits, Infrastructure — UNEP International Resource Panel](../../../materials/metals-and-metallurgical-production/sources/Metal-Recycling-UNEP-IRP.lingua#r_40JXFY43ST442BB8MJEAYJT9N1) and [The Materials Science behind Sustainable Metals and Alloys — Dierk Raabe](../sources/Materials-Science-behind-Sustainable-Metals-Raabe.lingua#r_6MXWN12M466MS374XY585GBHBN) for a metallic case, or [The U.S. Plastics Recycling Economy — Thomas, Kneifel and Butry](../sources/Plastics-Recycling-Economy-NIST.lingua#r_4FMXC9V02YNV4DFSCCV0CVR8JN) and complete primary methods for a polymer case; use [Recycled Concrete Aggregates: A Review — McNeil and Kang](../sources/Recycled-Concrete-Aggregates-McNeil-Kang.lingua#r_7RV5XYMDWNA5KPVRYC7052WV8E) and [Wood Handbook — Forest Products Laboratory, 2021](../sources/Wood-Handbook-FPL-2021.lingua#r_2SP2KMHCD78MQGZN69GKPGJ3WM) for an additional contrasting family.

Follow a multi-material product through use and two possible end-of-use routes. Reconstruct collection, separation, conversion and accepted-quality yields. Close consequential constituent balances and explain the next output functions. Define functional equivalence, boundary, data provenance, time and infrastructure requirements before comparing indicators.

**Deliver:** An independently checked inventory model, explicit multifunctionality treatment, lifetime/quality scenarios and sensitivity. Compare one conclusion across alternative allocation or substitution assumptions. Explain where retaining a component's structure changes the result and where additional processing creates useful quality. Distinguish environmental indicators from costs and judgments. Revise after a challenge to a principal data or counterfactual assumption.

**Return:** [Materials engineering — structure, processing and useful behavior](../Materials-engineering.lingua#r_05BF5JM8141RKF1VT5998YFZQ9).
**Continue in materials engineering:** [Defend the selection, service and recovery account](Defend-the-selection-service-and-recovery-account.lingua#r_3EKGFH7N9TS7SSRZHCP0MX6E8W).

